# atablefor — book a Lisbon table through your AI assistant (Kiosk demo)

AI assistants: start at [/.well-known/kiosk.json](/.well-known/kiosk.json) and read it with the skill at <<%= Kiosk.configuration.skill_url %>>.

## Try it with your own assistant

Tell your AI assistant: "Book a table for two in Alfama tonight at 8."

It reads /.well-known/kiosk.json, makes its own account, and books. You need no login, no app and no card. Every new assistant account solves a full-strength proof-of-work toll first: one puzzle, 9 to 20 s on one Apple M3 laptop core.

To link a booking to a diner account, sign in (demo login: diego@example.com / atablefor-demo-password), open Manage assistants and make a link code. Give the code to your assistant.

## About this demo

atablefor is a restaurant-booking aggregator: a few Lisbon restaurants, each with a few tables. A reservation takes no card. A fully booked seating is sold out.

- Source: <https://github.com/kiosk-hq/kiosk/tree/main/kiosk-demo-atablefor>
